DISCLAIMER

Proprietary research, not investment advice. Everything in this repository is
historical and observational evidence about how markets have behaved around FOMC
decisions. It is not a recommendation to buy or sell any security, it carries no
warranty of accuracy or fitness, and past reactions do not predict future ones.
Statistics reported here are tendencies on small samples (roughly 70 events);
none clears a conventional significance bar and no transaction costs are modeled.

THIRD-PARTY MATERIALS

U.S. Federal Reserve. FOMC statements, minutes, Summary of Economic Projections,
press-conference transcripts, and Board member speeches and testimony are works of
the U.S. Federal Reserve fetched from federalreserve.gov. They are U.S. government
works in the public domain. Extracted plain text is kept under data/fomc/<type>/text/;
the original HTML/PDF is not redistributed (git-ignored, reproducible with `fomc fetch`).

U.S. Senate. Kevin Warsh's confirmation opening statement and written Questions for
the Record responses were fetched from banking.senate.gov and are U.S. government
works.

FRED (Federal Reserve Bank of St. Louis). The balance-sheet and market-pricing axes
are computed from FRED series WALCL, WRESBAL, RRPONTSYD, DGS2, DGS10, T10Y2Y, DFF,
SOFR, IORB and WTREGEN, retrieved through the FRED API and cited per the FRED terms
of use (https://fred.stlouisfed.org/legal/). The repository stores only the latest
value, a 90-day change and a -1/0/+1 signal per indicator. The FRED series themselves
are not redistributed here.

SPY and TLT prices. Full price series are NOT redistributed. The event truth table
contains only per-event return percentages and the closing price on each of the
roughly 70 FOMC decision days. The full daily history is fetched at run time from
Yahoo Finance through the yfinance library into a git-ignored cache (data/market/).
Users are responsible for complying with Yahoo's terms of service.

Regime-intelligence news feed. apps/fomc-dashboard/public/data/regime_intel/ holds,
for each cited news item, only its title, URL, publisher, publication date, machine-
assigned scores, and two short fields (`evidence_text`, `why_it_matters`) that are
MACHINE-GENERATED PARAPHRASES produced by the collector (Perplexity `sonar` model)
under a contract that forbids verbatim quotation. They are not publisher text, they
are unverified, and they may misattribute. Article bodies are never stored. Titles
and other publisher metadata remain the property of their publishers and appear
here for citation.

Intentionally excluded. A Hoover Institution interview transcript ("Inflation Is a
Choice", 2025-07-08), two further Hoover items (the 2025 G30 lecture and a 2022
essay), and a Wall Street Journal op-ed by Kevin Warsh (2025-11-16) are copyrighted
and are not included. They are cited by URL only in
data/fomc/warsh/warsh_manifest.json.

Other referenced materials remain the property of their respective owners and are
used by summary or citation with attribution.
